    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ca",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3CA Nature of functions of magistrate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3ca"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A function of making an order conferred on a magistrate by\nsection 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN or 3ZQZB is conferred on the\nmagistrate in a personal capacity and not as a court or a member of\na court.\n\n(2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), an order made by\na magistrate under section 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN or 3ZQZB has\neffect only by virtue of this Act and is not to be taken by\nimplication to be made by a court.\n\n(3) A magistrate performing a function of, or connected with, making\nan order under section 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN or 3ZQZB has the\nsame protection and immunity as if he or she were performing that\nfunction as, or as a member of, a court (being the court of which\nthe magistrate is a member).\n\n(4) The Governor-General may make arrangements with the Governor\nof a State, the Chief Minister of the Australian Capital Territory or\nthe Administrator of the Northern Territory for the performance, by\nall or any of the persons who from time to time hold office as\nmagistrates in that State or Territory, of the function of making\norders under sections 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN and 3ZQZB.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A function of making an order conferred on a magistrate by\nsection 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN or 3ZQZB is conferred on the\nmagistrate in a personal capacity and not as a court or a member of\na court.\n\n(2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), an order made by\na magistrate under section 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN or 3ZQZB has\neffect only by virtue of this Act and is not to be taken by\nimplication to be made by a court.\n\n(3) A magistrate performing a function of, or connected with, making\nan order under section 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN or 3ZQZB has the\nsame protection and immunity as if he or she were performing that\nfunction as, or as a member of, a court (being the court of which\nthe magistrate is a member).\n\n(4) The Governor-General may make arrangements with the Governor\nof a State, the Chief Minister of the Australian Capital Territory or\nthe Administrator of the Northern Territory for the performance, by\nall or any of the persons who from time to time hold office as\nmagistrates in that State or Territory, of the function of making\norders under sections 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN and 3ZQZB.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ca-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ca-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ca-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ca-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "02eabe09a0bf81c025b05583374d14b10b1581d3a9341688d13177394e7ebd24"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3ca",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3CA Nature of functions of magistrate",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A function of making an order conferred on a magistrate by\nsection 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN or 3ZQZB is conferred on the\nmagistrate in a personal capacity and not as a court or a member of\na court.\n\n(2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), an order made by\na magistrate under section 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN or 3ZQZB has\neffect only by virtue of this Act and is not to be taken by\nimplication to be made by a court.\n\n(3) A magistrate performing a function of, or connected with, making\nan order under section 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN or 3ZQZB has the\nsame protection and immunity as if he or she were performing that\nfunction as, or as a member of, a court (being the court of which\nthe magistrate is a member).\n\n(4) The Governor-General may make arrangements with the Governor\nof a State, the Chief Minister of the Australian Capital Territory or\nthe Administrator of the Northern Territory for the performance, by\nall or any of the persons who from time to time hold office as\nmagistrates in that State or Territory, of the function of making\norders under sections 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN and 3ZQZB."
    },
