    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ca-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3CA(4) Nature of functions of magistrate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3ca-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Governor-General may make arrangements with the Governor\nof a State, the Chief Minister of the Australian Capital Territory or\nthe Administrator of the Northern Territory for the performance, by\nall or any of the persons who from time to time hold office as\nmagistrates in that State or Territory, of the function of making\norders under sections 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN and 3ZQZB.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The Governor-General may make arrangements with the Governor\nof a State, the Chief Minister of the Australian Capital Territory or\nthe Administrator of the Northern Territory for the performance, by\nall or any of the persons who from time to time hold office as\nmagistrates in that State or Territory, of the function of making\norders under sections 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN and 3ZQZB.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ca"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ca-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a04f7b52e78d8194d0dd743dda9b0461c458d9557e0ec79251749533753038ba",
      "skos:note": "Governor-General may make arrangements with other officials for magistrate performance"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3ca-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3CA(4) Nature of functions of magistrate",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Governor-General may make arrangements with the Governor\nof a State, the Chief Minister of the Australian Capital Territory or\nthe Administrator of the Northern Territory for the performance, by\nall or any of the persons who from time to time hold office as\nmagistrates in that State or Territory, of the function of making\norders under sections 3ZI, 3ZJ, 3ZK, 3ZN and 3ZQZB."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ca-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ca-ss-4"
