    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3d-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3D(6) Application of Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3d-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "(6) The application of this Part in relation to State offences that have a\nfederal aspect is not intended to limit or exclude the concurrent\noperation of any law of a State or of the Australian Capital\nTerritory.\nNote 1:\nSubsection 3(1) defines State to include the Northern Territory.\nNote 2:\nSection 3AA has the effect that an offence against the law of the\nAustralian Capital Territory is a State offence that has a federal aspect.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "skos:definition": "(6) The application of this Part in relation to State offences that have a\nfederal aspect is not intended to limit or exclude the concurrent\noperation of any law of a State or of the Australian Capital\nTerritory.\nNote 1:\nSubsection 3(1) defines State to include the Northern Territory.\nNote 2:\nSection 3AA has the effect that an offence against the law of the\nAustralian Capital Territory is a State offence that has a federal aspect.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3d-ss-6-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "37923bffce1f25512260dfe6e2a1064f3854a36a32dcd92e93cf48d3bba3a3cb",
      "skos:note": "Application of Part not intended to limit or exclude concurrent State laws"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3d-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3D(6) Application of Part",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "(6) The application of this Part in relation to State offences that have a\nfederal aspect is not intended to limit or exclude the concurrent\noperation of any law of a State or of the Australian Capital\nTerritory.\nNote 1:\nSubsection 3(1) defines State to include the Northern Territory.\nNote 2:\nSection 3AA has the effect that an offence against the law of the\nAustralian Capital Territory is a State offence that has a federal aspect.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)"
    },
    {
