    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3J Specific powers available to constables executing warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In executing a warrant in relation to premises, the executing officer\nor a constable assisting may:\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nSearch warrants  Division 2\n\nSection 3JA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) for a purpose incidental to the execution of the warrant; or\n\n(b) if the occupier of the premises consents in writing;\ntake photographs (including video recordings) of the premises or of\nthings at the premises.\n\n(2) If a warrant in relation to premises is being executed, the executing\nofficer and the constables assisting may, if the warrant is still in\nforce, complete the execution of the warrant after all of them\ntemporarily cease its execution and leave the premises:\n\n(a) for not more than one hour; or\n\n(aa) if there is an emergency situation, for not more than 12 hours\nor such longer period as allowed by an issuing officer under\nsection 3JA; or\n\n(b) for a longer period if the occupier of the premises consents in\nwriting.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the execution of a warrant is stopped by an order of a court;\nand\n\n(b) the order is later revoked or reversed on appeal; and\n\n(c) the warrant is still in force;\nthe execution of the warrant may be completed.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In executing a warrant in relation to premises, the executing officer\nor a constable assisting may:\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nSearch warrants  Division 2\n\nSection 3JA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) for a purpose incidental to the execution of the warrant; or\n\n(b) if the occupier of the premises consents in writing;\ntake photographs (including video recordings) of the premises or of\nthings at the premises.\n\n(2) If a warrant in relation to premises is being executed, the executing\nofficer and the constables assisting may, if the warrant is still in\nforce, complete the execution of the warrant after all of them\ntemporarily cease its execution and leave the premises:\n\n(a) for not more than one hour; or\n\n(aa) if there is an emergency situation, for not more than 12 hours\nor such longer period as allowed by an issuing officer under\nsection 3JA; or\n\n(b) for a longer period if the occupier of the premises consents in\nwriting.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the execution of a warrant is stopped by an order of a court;\nand\n\n(b) the order is later revoked or reversed on appeal; and\n\n(c) the warrant is still in force;\nthe execution of the warrant may be completed.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3j-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3j-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b93e221c0cb48c5a1f89698496a6b5649c497946b57bc922e1c2eacbe661b29a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3J Specific powers available to constables executing warrant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 56,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In executing a warrant in relation to premises, the executing officer\nor a constable assisting may:\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nSearch warrants  Division 2\n\nSection 3JA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) for a purpose incidental to the execution of the warrant; or\n\n(b) if the occupier of the premises consents in writing;\ntake photographs (including video recordings) of the premises or of\nthings at the premises.\n\n(2) If a warrant in relation to premises is being executed, the executing\nofficer and the constables assisting may, if the warrant is still in\nforce, complete the execution of the warrant after all of them\ntemporarily cease its execution and leave the premises:\n\n(a) for not more than one hour; or\n\n(aa) if there is an emergency situation, for not more than 12 hours\nor such longer period as allowed by an issuing officer under\nsection 3JA; or\n\n(b) for a longer period if the occupier of the premises consents in\nwriting.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the execution of a warrant is stopped by an order of a court;\nand\n\n(b) the order is later revoked or reversed on appeal; and\n\n(c) the warrant is still in force;\nthe execution of the warrant may be completed."
    },
