      "cml:premiseText": "(i) it is significantly more practicable..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3k-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3K(3) Use of equipment to examine or process things",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3k-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If a thing is moved to another place for the purpose of examination\nor processing under subsection (2), the executing officer must, if it\nis practicable to do so:\n\n(a) inform the person referred to in paragraph (2)(b) or (c) (as the\ncase requires) of the address of the place and the time at\nwhich the examination or processing will be carried out; and\n\n(b) allow that person or his or her representative to be present\nduring the examination or processing.\n\n(3AA) The executing officer need not comply with paragraph (3)(a) or (b)\nif he or she believes on reasonable grounds that to do so might:\n\n(a) endanger the safety of a person; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution.\nTime limit on moving a thing",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If a thing is moved to another place for the purpose of examination\nor processing under subsection (2), the executing officer must, if it\nis practicable to do so:\n\n(a) inform the person referred to in paragraph (2)(b) or (c) (as the\ncase requires) of the address of the place and the time at\nwhich the examination or processing will be carried out; and\n\n(b) allow that person or his or her representative to be present\nduring the examination or processing.\n\n(3AA) The executing officer need not comply with paragraph (3)(a) or (b)\nif he or she believes on reasonable grounds that to do so might:\n\n(a) endanger the safety of a person; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution.\nTime limit on moving a thing",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3k"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3k-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3k-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "931d83674064fc7a72ecb036c9f23e22101c0b563b8d82e028464c2831852da2",
      "skos:note": "Executing officer must inform and allow person to be present during examination or processing.",
      "dc:description": "Information about address and time of examination or processing"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3k-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3K(3) Use of equipment to examine or process things",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If a thing is moved to another place for the purpose of examination\nor processing under subsection (2), the executing officer must, if it\nis practicable to do so:\n\n(a) inform the person referred to in paragraph (2)(b) or (c) (as the\ncase requires) of the address of the place and the time at\nwhich the examination or processing will be carried out; and\n\n(b) allow that person or his or her representative to be present\nduring the examination or processing.\n\n(3AA) The executing officer need not comply with paragraph (3)(a) or (b)\nif he or she believes on reasonable grounds that to do so might:\n\n(a) endanger the safety of a person; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution.\nTime limit on moving a thing"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3k-ss-3-norm",
