    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3k-ss-3b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3K(3B) Use of equipment to examine or process things",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3k-ss-3b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "(3B) An executing officer may apply to an issuing officer for one or\nmore extensions of that time if the executing officer believes on\nreasonable grounds that the thing cannot be examined or processed\nwithin the time applicable under subsection (3A) or that time as\npreviously extended.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "skos:definition": "(3B) An executing officer may apply to an issuing officer for one or\nmore extensions of that time if the executing officer believes on\nreasonable grounds that the thing cannot be examined or processed\nwithin the time applicable under subsection (3A) or that time as\npreviously extended.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3k"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
