    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3la",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3LA Person with knowledge of a computer or a computer system to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3la"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.67",
      "values:originalText": "assist access etc.\n\n(1) A constable may apply to a magistrate for an order requiring a\nspecified person to provide any information or assistance that is\nreasonable and necessary to allow a constable to do one or more of\nthe following:\n\n(a) access data held in, or accessible from, a computer or data\nstorage device that:\n\n(i) is on warrant premises; or\n\n(ia) is found in the course of an ordinary search of a person,\nor a frisk search of a person, authorised by a warrant\nunder section 3E; or\n\n(ii) has been moved under subsection 3K(2) and is at a\nplace for examination or processing; or\n\n(iii) has been seized under this Division;\n\n(b) copy data held in, or accessible from, a computer, or data\nstorage device, described in paragraph (a) to another data\nstorage device;\n\n(c) convert into documentary form or another form intelligible to\na constable:\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "skos:definition": "assist access etc.\n\n(1) A constable may apply to a magistrate for an order requiring a\nspecified person to provide any information or assistance that is\nreasonable and necessary to allow a constable to do one or more of\nthe following:\n\n(a) access data held in, or accessible from, a computer or data\nstorage device that:\n\n(i) is on warrant premises; or\n\n(ia) is found in the course of an ordinary search of a person,\nor a frisk search of a person, authorised by a warrant\nunder section 3E; or\n\n(ii) has been moved under subsection 3K(2) and is at a\nplace for examination or processing; or\n\n(iii) has been seized under this Division;\n\n(b) copy data held in, or accessible from, a computer, or data\nstorage device, described in paragraph (a) to another data\nstorage device;\n\n(c) convert into documentary form or another form intelligible to\na constable:\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3la-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3la-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ec58f2d98a0938a9a54ea93f6e9630ddac86f9799b919900adac6c0fc10d7375",
      "skos:note": "A constable may apply for an order requiring a specified person to provide information or assistance.",
      "dc:description": "reasonable and necessary"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3la",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3LA Person with knowledge of a computer or a computer system to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 67,
      "values:originalText": "assist access etc.\n\n(1) A constable may apply to a magistrate for an order requiring a\nspecified person to provide any information or assistance that is\nreasonable and necessary to allow a constable to do one or more of\nthe following:\n\n(a) access data held in, or accessible from, a computer or data\nstorage device that:\n\n(i) is on warrant premises; or\n\n(ia) is found in the course of an ordinary search of a person,\nor a frisk search of a person, authorised by a warrant\nunder section 3E; or\n\n(ii) has been moved under subsection 3K(2) and is at a\nplace for examination or processing; or\n\n(iii) has been seized under this Division;\n\n(b) copy data held in, or accessible from, a computer, or data\nstorage device, described in paragraph (a) to another data\nstorage device;\n\n(c) convert into documentary form or another form intelligible to\na constable:\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3la-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3la"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
