    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3n",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3N Copies of seized things to be provided",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3n"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.72",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), if a constable seizes, under a warrant\nrelating to premises:\n\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n\n(b) a storage device the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthe constable must, if requested to do so by the occupier of the\npremises or another person who apparently represents the occupier\nand who is present when the warrant is executed, give a copy of the\nthing or the information to that person as soon as practicable after\nthe seizure.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the thing that has been seized was seized under\nsubsection 3L(1A) or paragraph 3L(2)(b) or 3LAA(4)(b); or\n\n(aaa) the thing that has been seized is a digital asset or a thing that\nsuggests the existence of a digital asset; or\n\n(aa) the thing embodies data that was accessed under the warrant\nat a place other than the premises; or\n\n(b) possession by the occupier of the document, film, computer\nfile, thing or information could constitute an offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), if a constable seizes, under a warrant\nrelating to premises:\n\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n\n(b) a storage device the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthe constable must, if requested to do so by the occupier of the\npremises or another person who apparently represents the occupier\nand who is present when the warrant is executed, give a copy of the\nthing or the information to that person as soon as practicable after\nthe seizure.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the thing that has been seized was seized under\nsubsection 3L(1A) or paragraph 3L(2)(b) or 3LAA(4)(b); or\n\n(aaa) the thing that has been seized is a digital asset or a thing that\nsuggests the existence of a digital asset; or\n\n(aa) the thing embodies data that was accessed under the warrant\nat a place other than the premises; or\n\n(b) possession by the occupier of the document, film, computer\nfile, thing or information could constitute an offence.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3n-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3n-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0dad266230b297b4312d077ee6abb9ded3cdf16d28d96d7d3718db872dd66dcd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3n",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3N Copies of seized things to be provided",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 72,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), if a constable seizes, under a warrant\nrelating to premises:\n\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n\n(b) a storage device the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthe constable must, if requested to do so by the occupier of the\npremises or another person who apparently represents the occupier\nand who is present when the warrant is executed, give a copy of the\nthing or the information to that person as soon as practicable after\nthe seizure.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the thing that has been seized was seized under\nsubsection 3L(1A) or paragraph 3L(2)(b) or 3LAA(4)(b); or\n\n(aaa) the thing that has been seized is a digital asset or a thing that\nsuggests the existence of a digital asset; or\n\n(aa) the thing embodies data that was accessed under the warrant\nat a place other than the premises; or\n\n(b) possession by the occupier of the document, film, computer\nfile, thing or information could constitute an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3n-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3N(1) Copies of seized things to be provided",
