      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.72",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the thing that has been seized was seized under\nsubsection 3L(1A) or paragraph 3L(2)(b) or 3LAA(4)(b); or\n\n(aaa) the thing that has been seized is a digital asset or a thing that\nsuggests the existence of a digital asset; or\n\n(aa) the thing embodies data that was accessed under the warrant\nat a place other than the premises; or\n\n(b) possession by the occupier of the document, film, computer\nfile, thing or information could constitute an offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the thing that has been seized was seized under\nsubsection 3L(1A) or paragraph 3L(2)(b) or 3LAA(4)(b); or\n\n(aaa) the thing that has been seized is a digital asset or a thing that\nsuggests the existence of a digital asset; or\n\n(aa) the thing embodies data that was accessed under the warrant\nat a place other than the premises; or\n\n(b) possession by the occupier of the document, film, computer\nfile, thing or information could constitute an offence.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3n"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3n-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "43436c1e987bf04fcc8eadedd2f5bf19dfcf1aa766dbd9d08af3e6a3f9a8d9df",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from seizure under subsection (1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3n-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3N(2) Copies of seized things to be provided",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 72,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the thing that has been seized was seized under\nsubsection 3L(1A) or paragraph 3L(2)(b) or 3LAA(4)(b); or\n\n(aaa) the thing that has been seized is a digital asset or a thing that\nsuggests the existence of a digital asset; or\n\n(aa) the thing embodies data that was accessed under the warrant\nat a place other than the premises; or\n\n(b) possession by the occupier of the document, film, computer\nfile, thing or information could constitute an offence."
    },
