    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3sa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3SA Relationship of this Division to parliamentary privileges and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3sa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.75",
      "values:originalText": "immunities\n\nTo avoid doubt, this Division does not affect the law relating to the\npowers, privileges and immunities of any of the following:\n\n(a) each House of the Parliament;\n\n(b) the members of each House of the Parliament;\n\n(c) the committees of each House of the Parliament and joint\ncommittees of both Houses of the Parliament.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "skos:definition": "immunities\n\nTo avoid doubt, this Division does not affect the law relating to the\npowers, privileges and immunities of any of the following:\n\n(a) each House of the Parliament;\n\n(b) the members of each House of the Parliament;\n\n(c) the committees of each House of the Parliament and joint\ncommittees of both Houses of the Parliament.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3sa-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3sa-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a0f4d1d938a455d4a2da313e8e679ea056cd9edb21566fa3e0b8aefceb10a0ae",
      "skos:note": "Exempts certain parliamentary powers and immunities from this Division."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3sa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3SA Relationship of this Division to parliamentary privileges and",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 75,
      "values:originalText": "immunities\n\nTo avoid doubt, this Division does not affect the law relating to the\npowers, privileges and immunities of any of the following:\n\n(a) each House of the Parliament;\n\n(b) the members of each House of the Parliament;\n\n(c) the committees of each House of the Parliament and joint\ncommittees of both Houses of the Parliament.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3sa-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3sa"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3sa-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "exemption",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Exempts certain entities from the scope of this Division.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "This Division does not affect...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the powers, privileges and immunities of any of the following:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3t",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3T Searches without warrant in emergency situations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3t"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.76",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if a constable suspects, on reasonable grounds,\nthat:\n\n(a) a thing relevant to an indictable offence is in or on a\nconveyance; and\n\n(b) it is necessary to exercise a power under subsection (2) in\norder to prevent the thing from being concealed, lost or\ndestroyed; and\n\n(c) it is necessary to exercise the power without the authority of\na search warrant because the circumstances are serious and\nurgent.\n\n(2) The constable may:\n\n(a) stop and detain the conveyance; and\n\n(b) search the conveyance and any container in or on the\nconveyance, for the thing; and\n\n(c) seize the thing if he or she finds it there.\n\n(3) If, in the course of searching for the thing, the constable finds\nanother thing relevant to an indictable offence or a thing relevant to\na summary offence, the constable may seize that thing if he or she\nsuspects, on reasonable grounds, that:\n\n(a) it is necessary to seize it in order to prevent its concealment,\nloss or destruction; and\n\n(b) it is necessary to seize it without the authority of a search\nwarrant because the circumstances are serious and urgent.\n\n(4) The constable must exercise his or her powers subject to\nsection 3U.\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nStopping and searching conveyances  Division 3\n\nSection 3U\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if a constable suspects, on reasonable grounds,\nthat:\n\n(a) a thing relevant to an indictable offence is in or on a\nconveyance; and\n\n(b) it is necessary to exercise a power under subsection (2) in\norder to prevent the thing from being concealed, lost or\ndestroyed; and\n\n(c) it is necessary to exercise the power without the authority of\na search warrant because the circumstances are serious and\nurgent.\n\n(2) The constable may:\n\n(a) stop and detain the conveyance; and\n\n(b) search the conveyance and any container in or on the\nconveyance, for the thing; and\n\n(c) seize the thing if he or she finds it there.\n\n(3) If, in the course of searching for the thing, the constable finds\nanother thing relevant to an indictable offence or a thing relevant to\na summary offence, the constable may seize that thing if he or she\nsuspects, on reasonable grounds, that:\n\n(a) it is necessary to seize it in order to prevent its concealment,\nloss or destruction; and\n\n(b) it is necessary to seize it without the authority of a search\nwarrant because the circumstances are serious and urgent.\n\n(4) The constable must exercise his or her powers subject to\nsection 3U.\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nStopping and searching conveyances  Division 3\n\nSection 3U\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3t-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3t-ss-2"
        },
