    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3t-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3T(4) Searches without warrant in emergency situations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3t-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.76",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The constable must exercise his or her powers subject to\nsection 3U.\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nStopping and searching conveyances  Division 3\n\nSection 3U\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The constable must exercise his or her powers subject to\nsection 3U.\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nStopping and searching conveyances  Division 3\n\nSection 3U\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3t"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3t-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3t-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8003a2662f0a01a0c58906c07921b52546996a63570357b465c7d143fbff071d",
      "skos:note": "No warrant required for searches in emergency situations"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3t-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3T(4) Searches without warrant in emergency situations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 76,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The constable must exercise his or her powers subject to\nsection 3U.\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nStopping and searching conveyances  Division 3\n\nSection 3U\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3t-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3t-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3t-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits warrantless searches",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3u",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3U How a constable exercises a power under section 3T",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3u"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.77",
      "values:originalText": "When a constable exercises a power under section 3T in relation to\na conveyance, he or she:\n\n(a) may use such assistance as is necessary; and\n\n(b) must search the conveyance in a public place or in some\nother place to which members of the public have ready\naccess; and\n\n(c) must not detain the conveyance for longer than is necessary\nand reasonable to search it and any container found in or on\nthe conveyance; and\n\n(d) may use such force as is necessary and reasonable in the\ncircumstances, but must not damage the conveyance or any\ncontainer found in or on the conveyance by forcing open a\npart of the conveyance or container unless:\n\n(i) the person (if any) apparently in charge of the\nconveyance has been given a reasonable opportunity to\nopen that part or container; or\n\n(ii) it is not possible to give that person such an opportunity.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "skos:definition": "When a constable exercises a power under section 3T in relation to\na conveyance, he or she:\n\n(a) may use such assistance as is necessary; and\n\n(b) must search the conveyance in a public place or in some\nother place to which members of the public have ready\naccess; and\n\n(c) must not detain the conveyance for longer than is necessary\nand reasonable to search it and any container found in or on\nthe conveyance; and\n\n(d) may use such force as is necessary and reasonable in the\ncircumstances, but must not damage the conveyance or any\ncontainer found in or on the conveyance by forcing open a\npart of the conveyance or container unless:\n\n(i) the person (if any) apparently in charge of the\nconveyance has been given a reasonable opportunity to\nopen that part or container; or\n\n(ii) it is not possible to give that person such an opportunity.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3u-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3u-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "782be3bd8d8cffd5120a3e3cca286613b8fd592395b155f1fdfffc4964316c80",
      "skos:note": "Constable must not detain conveyance for longer than necessary to search it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3u",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3U How a constable exercises a power under section 3T",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 77,
      "values:originalText": "When a constable exercises a power under section 3T in relation to\na conveyance, he or she:\n\n(a) may use such assistance as is necessary; and\n\n(b) must search the conveyance in a public place or in some\nother place to which members of the public have ready\naccess; and\n\n(c) must not detain the conveyance for longer than is necessary\nand reasonable to search it and any container found in or on\nthe conveyance; and\n\n(d) may use such force as is necessary and reasonable in the\ncircumstances, but must not damage the conveyance or any\ncontainer found in or on the conveyance by forcing open a\npart of the conveyance or container unless:\n\n(i) the person (if any) apparently in charge of the\nconveyance has been given a reasonable opportunity to\nopen that part or container; or\n\n(ii) it is not possible to give that person such an opportunity.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)"
    },
