    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ua",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3UA Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3ua"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "In this Division:\nassessment officer: see subsection 3UJC(1).\nCommonwealth place means a Commonwealth place within the\nmeaning of the Commonwealth Places (Application of Laws) Act\n1970.\nnominated ART member means a person in relation to whom a\nnomination is in force under section 3UJE.\npolice officer means:\n\n(a) a member of the Australian Federal Police (within the\nmeaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979); or\n\n(b) a special member (within the meaning of that Act); or\n\n(c) a member, however described, of a police force of a State or\nTerritory.\npost-entry warrant: see subsection 3UEB(1).\nprescribed security zone means a zone in respect of which a\ndeclaration under section 3UJ is in force.\nserious offence related item means a thing that a police officer\nconducting a search under section 3UD reasonably suspects:\n\n(a) may be used in a serious offence; or\n\n(b) is connected with the preparation for, or the engagement of a\nperson in, a serious offence; or\n\n(c) is evidence of, or relating to, a serious offence.\nState or Territory police oversight body means:\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nPowers in relation to terrorist acts and terrorism offences  Division 3A\n\nSection 3UB\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) an agency, body or authority that; or\n\n(b) a person who;\nunder a law of a State or Territory, has functions relating to the\ninvestigation of complaints about the conduct of members of the\npolice force of the State or Territory.\nterrorism related item means a thing that a police officer\nconducting a search under section 3UD reasonably suspects:\n\n(a) may be used in a terrorist act; or\n\n(b) is connected with the preparation for, or the engagement of a\nperson in, a terrorist act; or\n\n(c) is evidence of, or relating to, a terrorist act.\nvehicle includes any means of transport (and, without limitation,\nincludes a vessel and an aircraft).\nSubdivision B—Powers",
      "skos:definition": "In this Division:\nassessment officer: see subsection 3UJC(1).\nCommonwealth place means a Commonwealth place within the\nmeaning of the Commonwealth Places (Application of Laws) Act\n1970.\nnominated ART member means a person in relation to whom a\nnomination is in force under section 3UJE.\npolice officer means:\n\n(a) a member of the Australian Federal Police (within the\nmeaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979); or\n\n(b) a special member (within the meaning of that Act); or\n\n(c) a member, however described, of a police force of a State or\nTerritory.\npost-entry warrant: see subsection 3UEB(1).\nprescribed security zone means a zone in respect of which a\ndeclaration under section 3UJ is in force.\nserious offence related item means a thing that a police officer\nconducting a search under section 3UD reasonably suspects:\n\n(a) may be used in a serious offence; or\n\n(b) is connected with the preparation for, or the engagement of a\nperson in, a serious offence; or\n\n(c) is evidence of, or relating to, a serious offence.\nState or Territory police oversight body means:\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nPowers in relation to terrorist acts and terrorism offences  Division 3A\n\nSection 3UB\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) an agency, body or authority that; or\n\n(b) a person who;\nunder a law of a State or Territory, has functions relating to the\ninvestigation of complaints about the conduct of members of the\npolice force of the State or Territory.\nterrorism related item means a thing that a police officer\nconducting a search under section 3UD reasonably suspects:\n\n(a) may be used in a terrorist act; or\n\n(b) is connected with the preparation for, or the engagement of a\nperson in, a terrorist act; or\n\n(c) is evidence of, or relating to, a terrorist act.\nvehicle includes any means of transport (and, without limitation,\nincludes a vessel and an aircraft).\nSubdivision B—",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ua-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ua-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bfb543efda914be0e5963b8a0c48942a03b287d8f41f323cfd7b57ee493aab87",
      "skos:note": "Defines terms used in the Division."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3ua",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3UA Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "In this Division:\nassessment officer: see subsection 3UJC(1).\nCommonwealth place means a Commonwealth place within the\nmeaning of the Commonwealth Places (Application of Laws) Act\n1970.\nnominated ART member means a person in relation to whom a\nnomination is in force under section 3UJE.\npolice officer means:\n\n(a) a member of the Australian Federal Police (within the\nmeaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979); or\n\n(b) a special member (within the meaning of that Act); or\n\n(c) a member, however described, of a police force of a State or\nTerritory.\npost-entry warrant: see subsection 3UEB(1).\nprescribed security zone means a zone in respect of which a\ndeclaration under section 3UJ is in force.\nserious offence related item means a thing that a police officer\nconducting a search under section 3UD reasonably suspects:\n\n(a) may be used in a serious offence; or\n\n(b) is connected with the preparation for, or the engagement of a\nperson in, a serious offence; or\n\n(c) is evidence of, or relating to, a serious offence.\nState or Territory police oversight body means:\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nPowers in relation to terrorist acts and terrorism offences  Division 3A\n\nSection 3UB\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) an agency, body or authority that; or\n\n(b) a person who;\nunder a law of a State or Territory, has functions relating to the\ninvestigation of complaints about the conduct of members of the\npolice force of the State or Territory.\nterrorism related item means a thing that a police officer\nconducting a search under section 3UD reasonably suspects:\n\n(a) may be used in a terrorist act; or\n\n(b) is connected with the preparation for, or the engagement of a\nperson in, a terrorist act; or\n\n(c) is evidence of, or relating to, a terrorist act.\nvehicle includes any means of transport (and, without limitation,\nincludes a vessel and an aircraft).\nSubdivision B—Powers"
    },
    {
