        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ub-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "508e878dca5fe571e7a0fb305630539181b7e4defb3c857370e1f3d334cb15d7",
      "skos:note": "Police officer may request person to provide details. Police officer may exercise powers in relation to a person suspected of committing a terrorist act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3ub-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3UB(1) Application of Subdivision",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 79,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A police officer may exercise the powers under this Subdivision in\nrelation to a person if:\n\n(a) the person is in a Commonwealth place (other than a\nprescribed security zone) and the officer suspects on\nreasonable grounds that the person might have just\ncommitted, might be committing or might be about to\ncommit, a terrorist act; or\n\n(b) the person is in a Commonwealth place in a prescribed\nsecurity zone."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ub-ss-1-norm",
