    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ud-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3UD(4) Stopping and searching",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3ud-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In searching a thing (including a vehicle) under subsection (1), a\npolice officer may use such force as is reasonable and necessary in\nthe circumstances, but must not damage the thing by forcing it, or a\npart of it, open unless:\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In searching a thing (including a vehicle) under subsection (1), a\npolice officer may use such force as is reasonable and necessary in\nthe circumstances, but must not damage the thing by forcing it, or a\npart of it, open unless:\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ud"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ud-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ud-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1fb43c0cd013a679cc5f27f4460ac98c3fbab6079607e02e0f44a42ccc98c03f",
      "skos:note": "Police officer must not damage thing by forcing it open unless certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3ud-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3UD(4) Stopping and searching",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In searching a thing (including a vehicle) under subsection (1), a\npolice officer may use such force as is reasonable and necessary in\nthe circumstances, but must not damage the thing by forcing it, or a\npart of it, open unless:\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ud-ss-4-norm",
