      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ue-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits securing premises for longer than reasonably necessary without a warrant.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) Premises must not be secured under subsection (3) for longer than is reasonably necessary to obtain the warrant.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Securing premises for longer than reasonably necessary without a warrant is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ue-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3UE(5) Seizure of terrorism related items and serious offence related",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3ue-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "(5) In the course of searching for the thing, the police officer may also\nseize any other thing, or do anything to make the premises safe, if\nthe police officer suspects, on reasonable grounds, that it is\nnecessary to do so:\n\n(a) in order to protect a person’s life, health or safety; and\n\n(b) without the authority of a search warrant because the\ncircumstances are serious and urgent.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) In the course of searching for the thing, the police officer may also\nseize any other thing, or do anything to make the premises safe, if\nthe police officer suspects, on reasonable grounds, that it is\nnecessary to do so:\n\n(a) in order to protect a person’s life, health or safety; and\n\n(b) without the authority of a search warrant because the\ncircumstances are serious and urgent.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ue"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ue-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ue-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ue-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ue-ss-5-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ue-ss-5-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ue-ss-5-logic-argumentation-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d39d905fd7225dbb4fa620dde06e24c6dc7d19665a1221ee8f395cab1488ef1a",
      "skos:note": "Police may seize other items or take actions to make premises safe without a warrant if necessary for protecting life, health, or safety."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3ue-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3UE(5) Seizure of terrorism related items and serious offence related",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "(5) In the course of searching for the thing, the police officer may also\nseize any other thing, or do anything to make the premises safe, if\nthe police officer suspects, on reasonable grounds, that it is\nnecessary to do so:\n\n(a) in order to protect a person’s life, health or safety; and\n\n(b) without the authority of a search warrant because the\ncircumstances are serious and urgent."
    },
