    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ue-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3UE(7) Seizure of terrorism related items and serious offence related",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3ue-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "(7) If one or more police officers have entered premises in accordance\nwith this section, a police officer must, within 24 hours after the\nentry:\n\n(a) notify the occupier of the premises that the entry has taken\nplace; or\n\n(b) if it is not practicable so to notify the occupier—leave a\nwritten notice of the entry at the premises.\n3UEB  Emergency entry to premises without warrant—post-entry\nwarrants\nRequirement to apply for post-entry warrant",
      "skos:definition": "(7) If one or more police officers have entered premises in accordance\nwith this section, a police officer must, within 24 hours after the\nentry:\n\n(a) notify the occupier of the premises that the entry has taken\nplace; or\n\n(b) if it is not practicable so to notify the occupier—leave a\nwritten notice of the entry at the premises.\n3UEB  Emergency entry to premises without warrant—post-entry\nwarrants\nRequirement to apply for post-entry warrant",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ue"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
