      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3uo",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3UO Determination of airports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3uo"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.100",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine an airport\nfor the purposes of the definition of major airport in section 3UM.\n\n(2) A determination of an airport under subsection (1) must include a\ndescription of land in relation to the airport for the purposes of\nparagraph 3UM(2)(b).\n\n(3) This Division applies in relation to an airport determined under\nsubsection (1) only if the airport is ordinarily used for the purposes\nof any of the following:\n\n(a) flights that start or end in a Territory;\n\n(b) flights between Australia and a foreign country in which\naircraft are used in the course of trade or commerce, for the\ncarriage of passengers;\n\n(c) flights between one State and another State in which aircraft\nare used in the course of trade or commerce, for the carriage\nof passengers.\n\n(4) This Division may apply in relation to an airport determined under\nsubsection (1) even if the airport is also used for a purpose other\nthan a purpose mentioned in subsection (3).\nNote:\nSee also section 3UR (move-on directions at airports—alternative\nconstitutional scope).\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nIdentity information requirements, and move-on powers, at airports  Division 3B\n\nSection 3UP\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine an airport\nfor the purposes of the definition of major airport in section 3UM.\n\n(2) A determination of an airport under subsection (1) must include a\ndescription of land in relation to the airport for the purposes of\nparagraph 3UM(2)(b).\n\n(3) This Division applies in relation to an airport determined under\nsubsection (1) only if the airport is ordinarily used for the purposes\nof any of the following:\n\n(a) flights that start or end in a Territory;\n\n(b) flights between Australia and a foreign country in which\naircraft are used in the course of trade or commerce, for the\ncarriage of passengers;\n\n(c) flights between one State and another State in which aircraft\nare used in the course of trade or commerce, for the carriage\nof passengers.\n\n(4) This Division may apply in relation to an airport determined under\nsubsection (1) even if the airport is also used for a purpose other\nthan a purpose mentioned in subsection (3).\nNote:\nSee also section 3UR (move-on directions at airports—alternative\nconstitutional scope).\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nIdentity information requirements, and move-on powers, at airports  Division 3B\n\nSection 3UP\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
