    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3wa-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3WA(2) Constables’ power of arrest without warrant for a terrorism",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3wa-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.110",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n\n(a) a person has been arrested for an offence under\nsubsection (1); and\n\n(b) before the person is charged with the offence, the constable\nin charge of the investigation ceases to suspect on reasonable\ngrounds:\n\n(i) that the person committed the offence; or\n\n(ii) that holding the person in custody is necessary to\nachieve a purpose referred to in paragraph (1)(b);\nthe person must be released.\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nArrest and related matters  Division 4\n\nSection 3X\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If:\n\n(a) a person has been arrested for an offence under\nsubsection (1); and\n\n(b) before the person is charged with the offence, the constable\nin charge of the investigation ceases to suspect on reasonable\ngrounds:\n\n(i) that the person committed the offence; or\n\n(ii) that holding the person in custody is necessary to\nachieve a purpose referred to in paragraph (1)(b);\nthe person must be released.\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nArrest and related matters  Division 4\n\nSection 3X\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3wa"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3wa-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3wa-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0cd3d7000b412e28f048b78d6ee5e0a84da20f1e3da9783c3236a37c93bcfd7d",
      "skos:note": "Release person from custody if suspicion ceases on reasonable grounds."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3wa-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3WA(2) Constables’ power of arrest without warrant for a terrorism",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 110,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n\n(a) a person has been arrested for an offence under\nsubsection (1); and\n\n(b) before the person is charged with the offence, the constable\nin charge of the investigation ceases to suspect on reasonable\ngrounds:\n\n(i) that the person committed the offence; or\n\n(ii) that holding the person in custody is necessary to\nachieve a purpose referred to in paragraph (1)(b);\nthe person must be released.\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nArrest and related matters  Division 4\n\nSection 3X\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3wa-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
