    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3z",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3Z Power of arrest without warrant by other persons",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3z"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who is not a constable may, without warrant, arrest\nanother person if he or she believes on reasonable grounds that:\n\n(a) the other person is committing or has just committed an\nindictable offence; and\n\n(b) proceedings by summons against the other person would not\nachieve one or more of the purposes referred to in\nparagraph 3W(1)(b).\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nArrest and related matters  Division 4\n\nSection 3ZA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) A person who arrests another person under subsection (1) must, as\nsoon as practicable after the arrest, arrange for the other person,\nand any property found on the other person, to be delivered into the\ncustody of a constable.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person who is not a constable may, without warrant, arrest\nanother person if he or she believes on reasonable grounds that:\n\n(a) the other person is committing or has just committed an\nindictable offence; and\n\n(b) proceedings by summons against the other person would not\nachieve one or more of the purposes referred to in\nparagraph 3W(1)(b).\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nArrest and related matters  Division 4\n\nSection 3ZA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) A person who arrests another person under subsection (1) must, as\nsoon as practicable after the arrest, arrange for the other person,\nand any property found on the other person, to be delivered into the\ncustody of a constable.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3z-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3z-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7405285e2571de353bd19fae50cbd1b7c21e26d35b4e7189243ae9c845e2cfba"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3z",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3Z Power of arrest without warrant by other persons",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 112,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who is not a constable may, without warrant, arrest\nanother person if he or she believes on reasonable grounds that:\n\n(a) the other person is committing or has just committed an\nindictable offence; and\n\n(b) proceedings by summons against the other person would not\nachieve one or more of the purposes referred to in\nparagraph 3W(1)(b).\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nArrest and related matters  Division 4\n\nSection 3ZA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) A person who arrests another person under subsection (1) must, as\nsoon as practicable after the arrest, arrange for the other person,\nand any property found on the other person, to be delivered into the\ncustody of a constable."
    },
