    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3ZC Use of force in making arrest",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.115",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not, in the course of arresting another person for an\noffence, use more force, or subject the other person to greater\nindignity, than is necessary and reasonable to make the arrest or to\nprevent the escape of the other person after the arrest.\n\n(2) Without limiting the operation of subsection (1), a constable must\nnot, in the course of arresting a person for an offence:\n\n(a) do anything that is likely to cause the death of, or grievous\nbodily harm to, the person unless the constable believes on\nreasonable grounds that doing that thing is necessary to\nprotect life or to prevent serious injury to another person\n(including the constable); or\n\n(b) if the person is attempting to escape arrest by fleeing—do\nsuch a thing unless:\n\n(i) the constable believes on reasonable grounds that doing\nthat thing is necessary to protect life or to prevent\nserious injury to another person (including the\nconstable); and\n\n(ii) the person has, if practicable, been called on to\nsurrender and the constable believes on reasonable\ngrounds that the person cannot be apprehended in any\nother manner.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person must not, in the course of arresting another person for an\noffence, use more force, or subject the other person to greater\nindignity, than is necessary and reasonable to make the arrest or to\nprevent the escape of the other person after the arrest.\n\n(2) Without limiting the operation of subsection (1), a constable must\nnot, in the course of arresting a person for an offence:\n\n(a) do anything that is likely to cause the death of, or grievous\nbodily harm to, the person unless the constable believes on\nreasonable grounds that doing that thing is necessary to\nprotect life or to prevent serious injury to another person\n(including the constable); or\n\n(b) if the person is attempting to escape arrest by fleeing—do\nsuch a thing unless:\n\n(i) the constable believes on reasonable grounds that doing\nthat thing is necessary to protect life or to prevent\nserious injury to another person (including the\nconstable); and\n\n(ii) the person has, if practicable, been called on to\nsurrender and the constable believes on reasonable\ngrounds that the person cannot be apprehended in any\nother manner.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zc-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "615f8329c69a0a0209055b88792cf40edb52d9aaf7d3d297406f2e394eb33268"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3ZC Use of force in making arrest",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 115,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not, in the course of arresting another person for an\noffence, use more force, or subject the other person to greater\nindignity, than is necessary and reasonable to make the arrest or to\nprevent the escape of the other person after the arrest.\n\n(2) Without limiting the operation of subsection (1), a constable must\nnot, in the course of arresting a person for an offence:\n\n(a) do anything that is likely to cause the death of, or grievous\nbodily harm to, the person unless the constable believes on\nreasonable grounds that doing that thing is necessary to\nprotect life or to prevent serious injury to another person\n(including the constable); or\n\n(b) if the person is attempting to escape arrest by fleeing—do\nsuch a thing unless:\n\n(i) the constable believes on reasonable grounds that doing\nthat thing is necessary to protect life or to prevent\nserious injury to another person (including the\nconstable); and\n\n(ii) the person has, if practicable, been called on to\nsurrender and the constable believes on reasonable\ngrounds that the person cannot be apprehended in any\nother manner."
    },
