      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 116,
      "values:originalText": "A constable who arrests a person for an offence, or who is present\nat such an arrest, may, if the constable suspects on reasonable\ngrounds that the person is carrying:\n\n(a) evidential material in relation to that or another offence; or\n\n(b) a seizable item;\nconduct an ordinary search of the person at or soon after the time\nof arrest, and seize any such thing found as a result of the search."
    },
    {
