    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3ZH(2) Power to conduct an ordinary search or a strip search",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zh-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.117",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A strip search may be conducted if:\n\n(a) a constable suspects on reasonable grounds that the person\nhas in his or her possession:\n\n(i) a seizable item; or\n\n(ii) evidential material (other than forensic material as\ndefined in Part ID) in relation to that or another offence;\nand\n\n(b) the constable suspects on reasonable grounds that it is\nnecessary to conduct a strip search of the person in order to\nrecover that item or evidential material; and\n\n(c) a constable of the rank of superintendent or higher has\napproved the conduct of the search.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A strip search may be conducted if:\n\n(a) a constable suspects on reasonable grounds that the person\nhas in his or her possession:\n\n(i) a seizable item; or\n\n(ii) evidential material (other than forensic material as\ndefined in Part ID) in relation to that or another offence;\nand\n\n(b) the constable suspects on reasonable grounds that it is\nnecessary to conduct a strip search of the person in order to\nrecover that item or evidential material; and\n\n(c) a constable of the rank of superintendent or higher has\napproved the conduct of the search.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cb20410f1f4b7175c27b97ff28d32332550cd0c8f783ad9e573d5d4144b80ae3",
      "skos:note": "Conducting a strip search without reasonable grounds is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zh-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3ZH(2) Power to conduct an ordinary search or a strip search",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 117,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A strip search may be conducted if:\n\n(a) a constable suspects on reasonable grounds that the person\nhas in his or her possession:\n\n(i) a seizable item; or\n\n(ii) evidential material (other than forensic material as\ndefined in Part ID) in relation to that or another offence;\nand\n\n(b) the constable suspects on reasonable grounds that it is\nnecessary to conduct a strip search of the person in order to\nrecover that item or evidential material; and\n\n(c) a constable of the rank of superintendent or higher has\napproved the conduct of the search."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
