    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3ZH(2A) Power to conduct an ordinary search or a strip search",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zh-ss-2a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.117",
      "values:originalText": "(2A) If:\n\n(a) in the course of carrying out a strip search, the constable\ncomes to believe on reasonable grounds that the carrying out\nof a forensic procedure would be likely to produce evidence\nrelating to the offence for which the person has been arrested\nor any other offence; and\n\n(b) Part ID provides for the carrying out of such a forensic\nprocedure;\nthe forensic procedure must not be carried out except in accordance\nwith Part ID.",
      "skos:definition": "(2A) If:\n\n(a) in the course of carrying out a strip search, the constable\ncomes to believe on reasonable grounds that the carrying out\nof a forensic procedure would be likely to produce evidence\nrelating to the offence for which the person has been arrested\nor any other offence; and\n\n(b) Part ID provides for the carrying out of such a forensic\nprocedure;\nthe forensic procedure must not be carried out except in accordance\nwith Part ID.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "60b86c2afb64f9d37f5c72eb03bd1b17ded6d3fbce8b7450707eea919b1668fb",
      "skos:note": "Forensic procedure must not be carried out except in accordance with Part ID."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zh-ss-2a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3ZH(2A) Power to conduct an ordinary search or a strip search",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 117,
      "values:originalText": "(2A) If:\n\n(a) in the course of carrying out a strip search, the constable\ncomes to believe on reasonable grounds that the carrying out\nof a forensic procedure would be likely to produce evidence\nrelating to the offence for which the person has been arrested\nor any other offence; and\n\n(b) Part ID provides for the carrying out of such a forensic\nprocedure;\nthe forensic procedure must not be carried out except in accordance\nwith Part ID."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2a-norm",
