    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3ZH(2B) Power to conduct an ordinary search or a strip search",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zh-ss-2b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.117",
      "values:originalText": "(2B) The conducting of a strip search may include taking photographs of\nevidential material found on the person, whether or not taking\nphotographs is a forensic procedure provided for by Part ID.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "skos:definition": "(2B) The conducting of a strip search may include taking photographs of\nevidential material found on the person, whether or not taking\nphotographs is a forensic procedure provided for by Part ID.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "26c968995fb4907516711fd1151660e0658339632226a3d4cd57a2688ea3423f",
      "skos:note": "Conducting a strip search may include taking photographs of evidential material found on the person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zh-ss-2b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3ZH(2B) Power to conduct an ordinary search or a strip search",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 117,
      "values:originalText": "(2B) The conducting of a strip search may include taking photographs of\nevidential material found on the person, whether or not taking\nphotographs is a forensic procedure provided for by Part ID.\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2b-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2b"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zh-ss-2b-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Allows conducting a strip search.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
