        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zj-ss-3-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zj-ss-3-logic-argumentation-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5763c49682d2654bb9840085897d7da7b57242c4465ecb6ce6e42fdc1f92f713",
      "skos:note": "Constable may take identification material from a person in lawful custody with consent or reasonable grounds."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zj-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3ZJ(3) Taking fingerprints, recordings, samples of handwriting or",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 120,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If a person is in lawful custody in respect of an offence, a constable\nwho is of the rank of sergeant or higher or who is for the time\nbeing in charge of a police station may take identification material\nfrom the person, or cause identification material from the person to\nbe taken, if:\n\n(a) the person consents in writing; or\n\n(b) the constable believes on reasonable grounds that it is\nnecessary to do so to:\n\n(i) establish who the person is; or\n\n(ii) identify the person as the person who committed the\noffence; or\n\n(iii) provide evidence of, or relating to, the offence; or\n\n(ba) both of the following apply:\n\n(i) the identification material taken, or caused to be taken,\nis fingerprints or photographs (including video\nrecordings) of the person;\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nArrest and related matters  Division 4\n\nSection 3ZJ\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) the offence is punishable by imprisonment for a period\nof 12 months or more; or\n\n(c) the constable suspects on reasonable grounds that the person\nhas committed another offence and the identification material\nis to be taken for the purpose of identifying the person as the\nperson who committed the other offence or of providing\nevidence of, or relating to, the other offence."
    },
