    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zk",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3ZK Destruction of identification material",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zk"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.123",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) identification material has been taken from a person under\nsection 3ZJ; and\n\n(b) a period of 12 months has elapsed since the identification\nmaterial was taken; and\n\n(c) proceedings in respect of an offence to which the\ninvestigation material relates have not been instituted or have\nbeen discontinued;\nthe identification material must be destroyed as soon as practicable.\n\n(2) If identification material has been taken from a person under\nsection 3ZJ and:\n\n(a) the person is found to have committed an offence to which\nthe identification material relates but no conviction is\nrecorded; or\n\n(b) the person is acquitted of such an offence and:\n\n(i) no appeal is lodged against the acquittal; or\n\n(ii) an appeal is lodged against the acquittal and the\nacquittal is confirmed or the appeal is withdrawn;\nthe identification material must be destroyed as soon as practicable\nunless an investigation into, or a proceeding against the person for,\nanother offence to which the identification material relates is\npending.\n\n(3) A magistrate may, on application by a constable, extend the period\nof 12 months referred to in subsection (1) or that period as\npreviously extended under this subsection in relation to particular\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) identification material has been taken from a person under\nsection 3ZJ; and\n\n(b) a period of 12 months has elapsed since the identification\nmaterial was taken; and\n\n(c) proceedings in respect of an offence to which the\ninvestigation material relates have not been instituted or have\nbeen discontinued;\nthe identification material must be destroyed as soon as practicable.\n\n(2) If identification material has been taken from a person under\nsection 3ZJ and:\n\n(a) the person is found to have committed an offence to which\nthe identification material relates but no conviction is\nrecorded; or\n\n(b) the person is acquitted of such an offence and:\n\n(i) no appeal is lodged against the acquittal; or\n\n(ii) an appeal is lodged against the acquittal and the\nacquittal is confirmed or the appeal is withdrawn;\nthe identification material must be destroyed as soon as practicable\nunless an investigation into, or a proceeding against the person for,\nanother offence to which the identification material relates is\npending.\n\n(3) A magistrate may, on application by a constable, extend the period\nof 12 months referred to in subsection (1) or that period as\npreviously extended under this subsection in relation to particular\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zk-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zk-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zk-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3c3021c1edcbf46f77e2519705304501621461925c322a7c0dc26cd1e0fd4685"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zk",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3ZK Destruction of identification material",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 123,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) identification material has been taken from a person under\nsection 3ZJ; and\n\n(b) a period of 12 months has elapsed since the identification\nmaterial was taken; and\n\n(c) proceedings in respect of an offence to which the\ninvestigation material relates have not been instituted or have\nbeen discontinued;\nthe identification material must be destroyed as soon as practicable.\n\n(2) If identification material has been taken from a person under\nsection 3ZJ and:\n\n(a) the person is found to have committed an offence to which\nthe identification material relates but no conviction is\nrecorded; or\n\n(b) the person is acquitted of such an offence and:\n\n(i) no appeal is lodged against the acquittal; or\n\n(ii) an appeal is lodged against the acquittal and the\nacquittal is confirmed or the appeal is withdrawn;\nthe identification material must be destroyed as soon as practicable\nunless an investigation into, or a proceeding against the person for,\nanother offence to which the identification material relates is\npending.\n\n(3) A magistrate may, on application by a constable, extend the period\nof 12 months referred to in subsection (1) or that period as\npreviously extended under this subsection in relation to particular\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zk-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3ZK(1) Destruction of identification material",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zk-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
