    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zl",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3ZL Offence of refusing to allow identification material to be taken",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zl"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.124",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person is convicted of an offence, the judge or magistrate\npresiding at the proceedings at which the person was convicted\nmay order:\n\n(a) the person to attend a police station; or\n\n(b) that a constable be permitted to attend on the person in a\nplace of detention;\nwithin one month after the conviction to allow impressions of the\nperson’s fingerprints and/or or a photograph of the person to be\ntaken in accordance with the order.\n\n(2) A person must not refuse or fail to allow those impressions or a\nphotograph of the person to be taken.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(3A) The judge or magistrate may also make any other orders that are\nreasonably necessary for ensuring that the impressions of the\nperson’s fingerprints and/or a photograph of the person are taken in\naccordance with the order under subsection (1). For example, the\njudge or magistrate may order the person to attend a specified\npolice station at a specified time.\n\n(3B) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to an order under subsection (3A); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct contravenes the order.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nArrest and related matters  Division 4\n\nSection 3ZM\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3C) In this section:\nengage in conduct means:\n\n(a) do an act; or\n\n(b) omit to perform an act.\n\n(4) Nothing in this section derogates from the right to use the\nprovisions of Part ID as authority for the taking of fingerprints\nfrom a prescribed offender or a serious offender.\n\n(5) In subsection (4), prescribed offender and serious offender have\nthe meanings given in subsection 23WA(1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a person is convicted of an offence, the judge or magistrate\npresiding at the proceedings at which the person was convicted\nmay order:\n\n(a) the person to attend a police station; or\n\n(b) that a constable be permitted to attend on the person in a\nplace of detention;\nwithin one month after the conviction to allow impressions of the\nperson’s fingerprints and/or or a photograph of the person to be\ntaken in accordance with the order.\n\n(2) A person must not refuse or fail to allow those impressions or a\nphotograph of the person to be taken.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(3A) The judge or magistrate may also make any other orders that are\nreasonably necessary for ensuring that the impressions of the\nperson’s fingerprints and/or a photograph of the person are taken in\naccordance with the order under subsection (1). For example, the\njudge or magistrate may order the person to attend a specified\npolice station at a specified time.\n\n(3B) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to an order under subsection (3A); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct contravenes the order.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nArrest and related matters  Division 4\n\nSection 3ZM\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3C) In this section:\nengage in conduct means:\n\n(a) do an act; or\n\n(b) omit to perform an act.\n\n(4) Nothing in this section derogates from the right to use the\nprovisions of Part ID as authority for the taking of fingerprints\nfrom a prescribed offender or a serious offender.\n\n(5) In subsection (4), prescribed offender and serious offender have\nthe meanings given in subsection",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zl-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zl-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zl-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zl-ss-3a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zl-ss-3b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zl-ss-3c"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zl-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zl-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eee624ed316b3aef2550c931041dda7f741b803123e8dd6069d42c9f2f60a4fb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zl",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3ZL Offence of refusing to allow identification material to be taken",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 124,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person is convicted of an offence, the judge or magistrate\npresiding at the proceedings at which the person was convicted\nmay order:\n\n(a) the person to attend a police station; or\n\n(b) that a constable be permitted to attend on the person in a\nplace of detention;\nwithin one month after the conviction to allow impressions of the\nperson’s fingerprints and/or or a photograph of the person to be\ntaken in accordance with the order.\n\n(2) A person must not refuse or fail to allow those impressions or a\nphotograph of the person to be taken.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(3A) The judge or magistrate may also make any other orders that are\nreasonably necessary for ensuring that the impressions of the\nperson’s fingerprints and/or a photograph of the person are taken in\naccordance with the order under subsection (1). For example, the\njudge or magistrate may order the person to attend a specified\npolice station at a specified time.\n\n(3B) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to an order under subsection (3A); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct contravenes the order.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nArrest and related matters  Division 4\n\nSection 3ZM\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3C) In this section:\nengage in conduct means:\n\n(a) do an act; or\n\n(b) omit to perform an act.\n\n(4) Nothing in this section derogates from the right to use the\nprovisions of Part ID as authority for the taking of fingerprints\nfrom a prescribed offender or a serious offender.\n\n(5) In subsection (4), prescribed offender and serious offender have\nthe meanings given in subsection 23WA(1)."
    },
    {
