      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ee2f400cce8a070b1e53e2ecdc86d2e193298de235a64615abcc2a10547d4894",
      "skos:note": "Order to attend a police station or allow constable attendance for fingerprint/photograph taking after conviction."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zl-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3ZL(1) Offence of refusing to allow identification material to be taken",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 124,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person is convicted of an offence, the judge or magistrate\npresiding at the proceedings at which the person was convicted\nmay order:\n\n(a) the person to attend a police station; or\n\n(b) that a constable be permitted to attend on the person in a\nplace of detention;\nwithin one month after the conviction to allow impressions of the\nperson’s fingerprints and/or or a photograph of the person to be\ntaken in accordance with the order."
    },
    {
