        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Suspect agrees or requests"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zm-ss-2-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Reasonable circumstances require identification parade to be held",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "It is reasonable in the circumstances"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zm-ss-2a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3ZM(2A) Identification parades",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zm-ss-2a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.125",
      "values:originalText": "(2A) Without limiting the matters that may be taken into account in\ndetermining whether it is reasonable in the circumstances to hold\nan identification parade, the following must be taken into account:\n\n(a) the kind of offence, and the gravity of the offence,\nconcerned;\n\n(b) the likely importance in the circumstances of the evidence of\nidentification;\n\n(c) the practicality of holding an identification parade, having\nregard, among other things:\n\n(i) if the suspect fails to cooperate in the conduct of the\nparade—to the manner and extent of, and the reason (if\nany) for, the failure; and\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "skos:definition": "(2A) Without limiting the matters that may be taken into account in\ndetermining whether it is reasonable in the circumstances to hold\nan identification parade, the following must be taken into account:\n\n(a) the kind of offence, and the gravity of the offence,\nconcerned;\n\n(b) the likely importance in the circumstances of the evidence of\nidentification;\n\n(c) the practicality of holding an identification parade, having\nregard, among other things:\n\n(i) if the suspect fails to cooperate in the conduct of the\nparade—to the manner and extent of, and the reason (if\nany) for, the failure; and\n\n\nPart IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers\nunder delayed notification search warrants)",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zm"
      },
