          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zo-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zo-ss-1a-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zo-ss-1a-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zo-ss-1a-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zo-ss-1a-logic-descriptionlogic-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zo-ss-1a-logic-alleninterval-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1100e43d7ca739e53e33f958c0d95c3fa9726a5e1ce26e2afe40be2ab82e687c",
      "skos:note": "Must consider certain factors when deciding whether to hold an identification parade.",
      "dc:description": "Reasons for failure to cooperate in the conduct of the parade, and reasons for not making an identification."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zo-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3ZO(1A) Identification by means of photographs",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 130,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) Without limiting the matters that may be taken into account in\ndetermining whether it would be unreasonable in the circumstances\nto hold an identification parade, the following must be taken into\naccount:\n\n(a) the kind of offence, and the gravity of the offence,\nconcerned;\n\n(b) the likely importance in the circumstances of the evidence of\nidentification;\n\n(c) the practicality of holding an identification parade, having\nregard, among other things:\n\n\nSearch, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under\ndelayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA\nArrest and related matters  Division 4\n\nSection 3ZO\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) if the suspect fails to cooperate in the conduct of the\nparade—to the manner and extent of, and the reason (if\nany) for, the failure; and\n\n(ii) in any case—to whether an identification was made at\nor about the time of the commission of the offence; and\n\n(d) the appropriateness of holding an identification parade,\nhaving regard, among other things, to the relationship (if any)\nbetween the suspect and the person who may make an\nidentification at the identification parade."
    },
