      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.150",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 3ZQN or 3ZQO;\nand\n\n(b) the notice specifies that information about the notice must\nnot be disclosed; and\n\n(c) the person discloses the existence or nature of the notice.\nPenalty: 120 penalty units or imprisonment for 2 years, or both.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 3ZQN or 3ZQO;\nand\n\n(b) the notice specifies that information about the notice must\nnot be disclosed; and\n\n(c) the person discloses the existence or nature of the notice.\nPenalty: 120 penalty units or imprisonment for 2 years, or both.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-149"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-149-ss-1-norm"
        },
