      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zs",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3ZS Announcement before entry",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zs"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.164",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A constable must, before any person enters premises under a\nwarrant or to arrest a person:\n\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n\n(b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n\n(2) A constable is not required to comply with subsection (1) if he or\nshe believes on reasonable grounds that immediate entry to the\npremises is required to ensure:\n\n(a) the safety of a person (including a constable); or\n\n(b) that the effective execution of the warrant or the arrest is not\nfrustrated.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A constable must, before any person enters premises under a\nwarrant or to arrest a person:\n\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n\n(b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n\n(2) A constable is not required to comply with subsection (1) if he or\nshe believes on reasonable grounds that immediate entry to the\npremises is required to ensure:\n\n(a) the safety of a person (including a constable); or\n\n(b) that the effective execution of the warrant or the arrest is not\nfrustrated.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zs-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zs-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8a725d38ddf57376cdf8afef2f86b3ef2a534c06bb320d0e571e6bbc83f2c820"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-3zs",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3ZS Announcement before entry",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 164,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A constable must, before any person enters premises under a\nwarrant or to arrest a person:\n\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n\n(b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n\n(2) A constable is not required to comply with subsection (1) if he or\nshe believes on reasonable grounds that immediate entry to the\npremises is required to ensure:\n\n(a) the safety of a person (including a constable); or\n\n(b) that the effective execution of the warrant or the arrest is not\nfrustrated."
    },
