    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4ab",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4AB Conversion of pecuniary penalties expressed in dollar amounts",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-4ab"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.329",
      "values:originalText": "to penalty units\n\n(1) A reference in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory\nOrdinance to a pecuniary penalty of D dollars, where D is a\nnumber, is taken to be a reference to a pecuniary penalty of P\npenalty units, where P is:\n\n(a) if D   100 is a whole number—that whole number; or\n\n(b) if D   100 is not a whole number—the next highest whole\nnumber.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a reference to the maximum\namount of a penalty that is not imposed by a court, or by a service\ntribunal under the Defence Force Discipline Act 1982.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply to:\n\n(a) section 76 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; or\n\n(c) a provision of a law of the Commonwealth prescribed for the\npurposes of this subsection.\n\n(4) In this section:\npenalty includes a fine.\nTerritory Ordinance has the same meaning as in section 4AA.",
      "skos:definition": "to penalty units\n\n(1) A reference in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory\nOrdinance to a pecuniary penalty of D dollars, where D is a\nnumber, is taken to be a reference to a pecuniary penalty of P\npenalty units, where P is:\n\n(a) if D   100 is a whole number—that whole number; or\n\n(b) if D   100 is not a whole number—the next highest whole\nnumber.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a reference to the maximum\namount of a penalty that is not imposed by a court, or by a service\ntribunal under the Defence Force Discipline Act 1982.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply to:\n\n(a) section 76 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; or\n\n(c) a provision of a law of the Commonwealth prescribed for the\npurposes of this subsection.\n\n(4) In this section:\npenalty includes a fine.\nTerritory Ordinance has the same meaning as in section 4AA.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4ab-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4ab-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4ab-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4ab-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bca2c22445edafec619227394a73cfbb7e24503f92e4c1b02187f331304a95b6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-4ab",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4AB Conversion of pecuniary penalties expressed in dollar amounts",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 329,
      "values:originalText": "to penalty units\n\n(1) A reference in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory\nOrdinance to a pecuniary penalty of D dollars, where D is a\nnumber, is taken to be a reference to a pecuniary penalty of P\npenalty units, where P is:\n\n(a) if D   100 is a whole number—that whole number; or\n\n(b) if D   100 is not a whole number—the next highest whole\nnumber.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a reference to the maximum\namount of a penalty that is not imposed by a court, or by a service\ntribunal under the Defence Force Discipline Act 1982.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply to:\n\n(a) section 76 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; or\n\n(c) a provision of a law of the Commonwealth prescribed for the\npurposes of this subsection.\n\n(4) In this section:\npenalty includes a fine.\nTerritory Ordinance has the same meaning as in section 4AA."
    },
