      "values:originalText": "(2) Where an act or omission constitutes an offence under both:\n\n(a) a law of the Commonwealth and a law of a State; or\n\n(b) a law of the Commonwealth and a law of a Territory;\nand the offender has been punished for that offence under the law\nof the State or the law of the Territory, as the case may be, the\noffender shall not be liable to be punished for the offence under the\nlaw of the Commonwealth.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Where an act or omission constitutes an offence under both:\n\n(a) a law of the Commonwealth and a law of a State; or\n\n(b) a law of the Commonwealth and a law of a Territory;\nand the offender has been punished for that offence under the law\nof the State or the law of the Territory, as the case may be, the\noffender shall not be liable to be punished for the offence under the\nlaw of the Commonwealth.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-2-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-2-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-2-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9bf92fe0a229c7cef08d583262bb65ced0d9507f102b95c8a14d8fa9bfe7d135",
      "skos:note": "Offender not liable for Commonwealth offence if already punished under State or Territory law."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-4c-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4C(2) Offences under 2 or more laws",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 331,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Where an act or omission constitutes an offence under both:\n\n(a) a law of the Commonwealth and a law of a State; or\n\n(b) a law of the Commonwealth and a law of a Territory;\nand the offender has been punished for that offence under the law\nof the State or the law of the Territory, as the case may be, the\noffender shall not be liable to be punished for the offence under the\nlaw of the Commonwealth."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "If offender not liable, then Commonwealth offence cannot be committed.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(not (offender liable to Commonwealth law)) -> (not (Commonwealth offence committed))",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(offender not liable to Commonwealth law) -> (offender not punished for Commonwealth offence)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Offence under multiple laws overlaps in time.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(Commonwealth offence) ∩ (State offence) ≠ ∅ ∧ (Commonwealth offence) ∩ (Territory offence) ≠ ∅",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(offender not punished for Commonwealth offence) -> (offender not liable to Commonwealth law)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-2-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Until",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Offence under multiple laws occurs until offender is punished.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(Commonwealth offence) ∩ (State offence) ≠ ∅ ∧ (offender not punished for Commonwealth offence)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(offender not liable to Commonwealth law) -> (offender not punished for Commonwealth offence)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-2-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Diffuses",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Offence under multiple laws diffuses through time.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(Commonwealth offence) ∩ (State offence) ≠ ∅ ∧ (offender not punished for Commonwealth offence)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(offender not liable to Commonwealth law) -> (offender not punished for Commonwealth offence)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-2-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recognizes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Offence under multiple laws recognized by AI.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(Commonwealth offence) ∩ (State offence) ≠ ∅ ∧ (offender not punished for Commonwealth offence)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(offender not liable to Commonwealth law) -> (offender not punished for Commonwealth offence)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4C(3) Offences under 2 or more laws",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-4c-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.331",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Where an act or omission constitutes an offence against a law of a\nTerritory, the validity of that law is not affected merely because the\nact or omission also constitutes an offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Where an act or omission constitutes an offence against a law of a\nTerritory, the validity of that law is not affected merely because the\nact or omission also constitutes an offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d6c9e44b3aaa6a9aba67ce9de74ef1475d49e7e01e66068f5d3b1504636f8a94",
      "skos:note": "Validity of a law is not affected by concurrent offences against other laws."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-4c-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4C(3) Offences under 2 or more laws",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 331,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Where an act or omission constitutes an offence against a law of a\nTerritory, the validity of that law is not affected merely because the\nact or omission also constitutes an offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4c-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to uphold the law",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The validity of a law is not affected.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Therefore, it is an obligation to uphold the law."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4D Penalties",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-4d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.332",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Except so far as the contrary intention appears, a penalty, whether\npecuniary or otherwise, set out at the foot of any provision of an\nAct as described in a paragraph of subsection (1A) indicates:\n\n(a) if the provision expressly creates an offence—that the\noffence is punishable on conviction by a penalty not\nexceeding the penalty so set out; or\n\n(b) in any other case—that contravention of the provision is an\noffence against the provision, punishable on conviction by a\npenalty not exceeding the penalty so set out.\n\n(1A) Subsection (1) applies to a penalty set out:\n\n(a) at the foot of a section of an Act; or\n\n(b) at the foot of a subsection of an Act, but not at the foot of the\nsection containing the subsection; or\n\n(c) at the foot of a clause of any Schedule to an Act; or\n\n(d) at the foot of a subclause of any Schedule to an Act, but not\nat the foot of the clause containing the subclause.\n\n(1B) Subsection (1) does not affect the operation of subsection 4B(2),\n(2A) or (3).\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies to any instrument made under an Act\n(including rules, regulations or by-laws but not including a law of a\nTerritory) as if the instrument were an Act and as if each such rule,\nregulation or by-law were a section of an Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Except so far as the contrary intention appears, a penalty, whether\npecuniary or otherwise, set out at the foot of any provision of an\nAct as described in a paragraph of subsection (1A) indicates:\n\n(a) if the provision expressly creates an offence—that the\noffence is punishable on conviction by a penalty not\nexceeding the penalty so set out; or\n\n(b) in any other case—that contravention of the provision is an\noffence against the provision, punishable on conviction by a\npenalty not exceeding the penalty so set out.\n\n(1A) Subsection (1) applies to a penalty set out:\n\n(a) at the foot of a section of an Act; or\n\n(b) at the foot of a subsection of an Act, but not at the foot of the\nsection containing the subsection; or\n\n(c) at the foot of a clause of any Schedule to an Act; or\n\n(d) at the foot of a subclause of any Schedule to an Act, but not\nat the foot of the clause containing the subclause.\n\n(1B) Subsection (1) does not affect the operation of subsection 4B(2),\n(2A) or (3).\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies to any instrument made under an Act\n(including rules, regulations or by-laws but not including a law of a\nTerritory) as if the instrument were an Act and as if each such rule,\nregulation or by-law were a section of an Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4d-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4d-ss-1b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4d-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4d-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6cd13586ddc1f3fcde60d0d0e98dd5f7151029281e18dc4f1e4a056a28bd126b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-4d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4D Penalties",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 332,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Except so far as the contrary intention appears, a penalty, whether\npecuniary or otherwise, set out at the foot of any provision of an\nAct as described in a paragraph of subsection (1A) indicates:\n\n(a) if the provision expressly creates an offence—that the\noffence is punishable on conviction by a penalty not\nexceeding the penalty so set out; or\n\n(b) in any other case—that contravention of the provision is an\noffence against the provision, punishable on conviction by a\npenalty not exceeding the penalty so set out.\n\n(1A) Subsection (1) applies to a penalty set out:\n\n(a) at the foot of a section of an Act; or\n\n(b) at the foot of a subsection of an Act, but not at the foot of the\nsection containing the subsection; or\n\n(c) at the foot of a clause of any Schedule to an Act; or\n\n(d) at the foot of a subclause of any Schedule to an Act, but not\nat the foot of the clause containing the subclause.\n\n(1B) Subsection (1) does not affect the operation of subsection 4B(2),\n(2A) or (3).\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies to any instrument made under an Act\n(including rules, regulations or by-laws but not including a law of a\nTerritory) as if the instrument were an Act and as if each such rule,\nregulation or by-law were a section of an Act."
    },
