    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4J Certain indictable offences may be dealt with summarily",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-4j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.333",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an indictable offence (other than an\noffence referred to in subsection (4)) against a law of the\nCommonwealth, being an offence punishable by imprisonment for\na period not exceeding 10 years, may, unless the contrary intention\nappears, be heard and determined, with the consent of the\nprosecutor and the defendant, by a court of summary jurisdiction.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to an indictable offence\nwhere, under a law of the Commonwealth other than this Act, that\noffence may be heard and determined by a court of summary\njurisdiction.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an indictable offence (other than an\noffence referred to in subsection (4)) against a law of the\nCommonwealth, being an offence punishable by imprisonment for\na period not exceeding 10 years, may, unless the contrary intention\nappears, be heard and determined, with the consent of the\nprosecutor and the defendant, by a court of summary jurisdiction.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to an indictable offence\nwhere, under a law of the Commonwealth other than this Act, that\noffence may be heard and determined by a court of summary\njurisdiction.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4j-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a646836f6da1e39eec082172c8f68174bf7b07d8384ddfd5f54e60d1f0346883"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-4j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4J Certain indictable offences may be dealt with summarily",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 333,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an indictable offence (other than an\noffence referred to in subsection (4)) against a law of the\nCommonwealth, being an offence punishable by imprisonment for\na period not exceeding 10 years, may, unless the contrary intention\nappears, be heard and determined, with the consent of the\nprosecutor and the defendant, by a court of summary jurisdiction.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to an indictable offence\nwhere, under a law of the Commonwealth other than this Act, that\noffence may be heard and determined by a court of summary\njurisdiction."
    },
