    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4ja",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4JA Some indictable offences punishable by fine only may be dealt",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-4ja"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.335",
      "values:originalText": "with summarily\n\n(1) A court of summary jurisdiction may hear and determine an\nindictable offence if:\n\n(a) the offence is not punishable by imprisonment; and\n\n(b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than 600\npenalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a\nbody corporate; and\n\n(c) the defendant and prosecution consent.\n\n(2) If the defendant is convicted, the court may impose a pecuniary\npenalty of:\n\n(a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300\npenalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be\npunishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more\nthan 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty\nunits for a body corporate; or\n\n(b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600\npenalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be\npunishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more\nthan 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty\nunits for a body corporate.\nHowever, the court may not impose a pecuniary penalty greater\nthan the penalty that could have been imposed if the offence had\nbeen prosecuted on indictment.\n\n(3) This section has effect subject to any contrary intention indicated\nby the law creating the offence.\n\n(4) Without limiting subsection (3), this section does not apply to an\nindictable offence:",
      "skos:definition": "with summarily\n\n(1) A court of summary jurisdiction may hear and determine an\nindictable offence if:\n\n(a) the offence is not punishable by imprisonment; and\n\n(b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than 600\npenalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a\nbody corporate; and\n\n(c) the defendant and prosecution consent.\n\n(2) If the defendant is convicted, the court may impose a pecuniary\npenalty of:\n\n(a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300\npenalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be\npunishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more\nthan 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty\nunits for a body corporate; or\n\n(b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600\npenalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be\npunishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more\nthan 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty\nunits for a body corporate.\nHowever, the court may not impose a pecuniary penalty greater\nthan the penalty that could have been imposed if the offence had\nbeen prosecuted on indictment.\n\n(3) This section has effect subject to any contrary intention indicated\nby the law creating the offence.\n\n(4) Without limiting subsection (3), this section does not apply to an\nindictable offence:",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4ja-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4ja-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4ja-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4ja-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eea591ee022001839297adbf7f7411706dc348815a08e89e6130150777121555"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-4ja",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4JA Some indictable offences punishable by fine only may be dealt",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 335,
      "values:originalText": "with summarily\n\n(1) A court of summary jurisdiction may hear and determine an\nindictable offence if:\n\n(a) the offence is not punishable by imprisonment; and\n\n(b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than 600\npenalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a\nbody corporate; and\n\n(c) the defendant and prosecution consent.\n\n(2) If the defendant is convicted, the court may impose a pecuniary\npenalty of:\n\n(a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300\npenalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be\npunishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more\nthan 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty\nunits for a body corporate; or\n\n(b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600\npenalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be\npunishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more\nthan 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty\nunits for a body corporate.\nHowever, the court may not impose a pecuniary penalty greater\nthan the penalty that could have been imposed if the offence had\nbeen prosecuted on indictment.\n\n(3) This section has effect subject to any contrary intention indicated\nby the law creating the offence.\n\n(4) Without limiting subsection (3), this section does not apply to an\nindictable offence:"
    },
