      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.337",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Any constable may, without warrant, seize any articles which are\nforfeited or which he or she has reasonable ground to believe are\nforfeited under any law of the Commonwealth, and take them\nbefore a court of summary jurisdiction.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Any constable may, without warrant, seize any articles which are\nforfeited or which he or she has reasonable ground to believe are\nforfeited under any law of the Commonwealth, and take them\nbefore a court of summary jurisdiction.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4beaf510a21c4b51039508e55e39f06e476663be47309c346a94f7dac4b4bf89",
      "skos:note": "Seizure of forfeitable goods is prohibited without warrant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-9-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9(1) Seizure and condemnation of forfeitable goods",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 337,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Any constable may, without warrant, seize any articles which are\nforfeited or which he or she has reasonable ground to believe are\nforfeited under any law of the Commonwealth, and take them\nbefore a court of summary jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9(2) Seizure and condemnation of forfeitable goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-9-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.337",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Where articles are taken before a court of summary jurisdiction\nunder subsection (1), the court shall inquire into the matter and:\n\n(a) if the court is satisfied that the articles are forfeited—shall\norder that the articles be condemned; or\n\n(b) if the court is not so satisfied—shall order that the articles be\ndelivered to such person as the court is satisfied is entitled to\nthe articles.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Where articles are taken before a court of summary jurisdiction\nunder subsection (1), the court shall inquire into the matter and:\n\n(a) if the court is satisfied that the articles are forfeited—shall\norder that the articles be condemned; or\n\n(b) if the court is not so satisfied—shall order that the articles be\ndelivered to such person as the court is satisfied is entitled to\nthe articles.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bfc591fdaa7962184c86c19f0851114fac176be1ad9fa54d050b46133c3e4039",
      "skos:note": "Articles cannot be delivered if they are forfeited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-9-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9(2) Seizure and condemnation of forfeitable goods",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 337,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Where articles are taken before a court of summary jurisdiction\nunder subsection (1), the court shall inquire into the matter and:\n\n(a) if the court is satisfied that the articles are forfeited—shall\norder that the articles be condemned; or\n\n(b) if the court is not so satisfied—shall order that the articles be\ndelivered to such person as the court is satisfied is entitled to\nthe articles."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits delivery of articles if they are forfeited.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) Where articles are taken before a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (1), the court shall inquire into the matter and:",
      "cml:conclusionText": "shall order that the articles be delivered to such person as the court is satisfied is entitled to the articles."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9A Forfeited articles to be dealt with by Official Trustee",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-9a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.338",
      "values:originalText": "Where articles are transferred to the Official Trustee under\nsubsection 9(4), the Official Trustee must, subject to any direction\nby the Minister administering the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002\ngiven in a particular case:\n\n(a) sell or otherwise dispose of the articles; and\n\n(b) apply the proceeds of the sale or disposition in payment of\nthe Official Trustee’s remuneration and other costs, charges\nand expenses of the kind referred to in section 9B payable to\nor incurred by it in connection with the sale or disposition;\nand\n\n(c) credit the remainder of those proceeds to the Confiscated\nAssets Account as required by section 296 of the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002.",
      "skos:definition": "Where articles are transferred to the Official Trustee under\nsubsection 9(4), the Official Trustee must, subject to any direction\nby the Minister administering the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002\ngiven in a particular case:\n\n(a) sell or otherwise dispose of the articles; and\n\n(b) apply the proceeds of the sale or disposition in payment of\nthe Official Trustee’s remuneration and other costs, charges\nand expenses of the kind referred to in section 9B payable to\nor incurred by it in connection with the sale or disposition;\nand\n\n(c) credit the remainder of those proceeds to the Confiscated\nAssets Account as required by section 296 of the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "de998dfa1007ef89716851931a341db09466ec92bf184789bf29d458057d401e",
      "skos:note": "Official Trustee must sell or dispose of forfeited articles and apply proceeds to remuneration and costs."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-9a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9A Forfeited articles to be dealt with by Official Trustee",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 338,
      "values:originalText": "Where articles are transferred to the Official Trustee under\nsubsection 9(4), the Official Trustee must, subject to any direction\nby the Minister administering the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002\ngiven in a particular case:\n\n(a) sell or otherwise dispose of the articles; and\n\n(b) apply the proceeds of the sale or disposition in payment of\nthe Official Trustee’s remuneration and other costs, charges\nand expenses of the kind referred to in section 9B payable to\nor incurred by it in connection with the sale or disposition;\nand\n\n(c) credit the remainder of those proceeds to the Confiscated\nAssets Account as required by section 296 of the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Official Trustee must perform action.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9B Costs etc. payable to Official Trustee",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-9b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.338",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may make provision in relation to:\n\n(a) the costs, charges and expenses incurred in connection with;\nand\n\n(b) the Official Trustee’s remuneration in respect of;\nthe performance or exercise by the Official Trustee of functions,\nduties or powers under section 9A.\n\n\nGeneral  Part IA\n\nSection 13\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) An amount equal to each amount of remuneration that the Official\nTrustee receives under the regulations is to be paid to the\nCommonwealth.\n\n(3) Where there are no regulations in relation to a matter referred to in\nsubsection (1):\n\n(a) the regulations referred to in section 288 of the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002 apply, so far as they are applicable, and with\nappropriate changes, in relation to the matter; and\n\n(b) a reference in subsection (1) or (2) to regulations is taken to\nbe a reference to the regulations referred to in section 288 of\nthe Proceeds of Crime Act 2002.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The regulations may make provision in relation to:\n\n(a) the costs, charges and expenses incurred in connection with;\nand\n\n(b) the Official Trustee’s remuneration in respect of;\nthe performance or exercise by the Official Trustee of functions,\nduties or powers under section 9A.\n\n\nGeneral  Part IA\n\nSection 13\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) An amount equal to each amount of remuneration that the Official\nTrustee receives under the regulations is to be paid to the\nCommonwealth.\n\n(3) Where there are no regulations in relation to a matter referred to in\nsubsection (1):\n\n(a) the regulations referred to in section 288 of the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002 apply, so far as they are applicable, and with\nappropriate changes, in relation to the matter; and\n\n(b) a reference in subsection (1) or (2) to regulations is taken to\nbe a reference to the regulations referred to in section 288 of\nthe Proceeds of Crime Act 2002.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7579f5f9993d05196249eb2bf1a041873a92cfb9746fdfb8445b1de920584904"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-9b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9B Costs etc. payable to Official Trustee",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 338,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may make provision in relation to:\n\n(a) the costs, charges and expenses incurred in connection with;\nand\n\n(b) the Official Trustee’s remuneration in respect of;\nthe performance or exercise by the Official Trustee of functions,\nduties or powers under section 9A.\n\n\nGeneral  Part IA\n\nSection 13\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) An amount equal to each amount of remuneration that the Official\nTrustee receives under the regulations is to be paid to the\nCommonwealth.\n\n(3) Where there are no regulations in relation to a matter referred to in\nsubsection (1):\n\n(a) the regulations referred to in section 288 of the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002 apply, so far as they are applicable, and with\nappropriate changes, in relation to the matter; and\n\n(b) a reference in subsection (1) or (2) to regulations is taken to\nbe a reference to the regulations referred to in section 288 of\nthe Proceeds of Crime Act 2002."
    },
