      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite any other law of the Commonwealth, a bail authority must\nnot grant bail to a person covered by subsection (2) or (2A), in\nrelation to an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, unless\nthe bail authority is satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist to\njustify bail.\nNote:\nFor persons under 18 years of age, see subsection (3AA).\nPersons covered by this section",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Despite any other law of the Commonwealth, a bail authority must\nnot grant bail to a person covered by subsection (2) or (2A), in\nrelation to an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, unless\nthe bail authority is satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist to\njustify bail.\nNote:\nFor persons under 18 years of age, see subsection (3AA).\nPersons covered by this section",
