    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15aa-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15AA(3) Bail not to be granted in certain cases",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15aa-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.340",
      "values:originalText": "(3) To avoid doubt, the express reference in paragraph (2)(d) to an\nancillary offence does not imply that references in\nparagraphs (2)(a), (b) or (c) to an offence do not include references\nto ancillary offences.\nEntering reasons in court records if court grants bail\n\n(3AAA) If the bail authority is a court and it grants bail, the court must:\n\n(a) state its reasons; and\n\n(b) cause those reasons to be entered in the court’s records.\nDetermining exceptional circumstances in relation to persons\nunder 18 years of age\n\n(3AA) In determining whether exceptional circumstances exist to justify\ngranting bail to a person who is under 18 years of age, without\nlimiting the matters the bail authority may have regard to, the bail\nauthority must have regard to:\n\n(a) the protection of the community as the paramount\nconsideration; and\n\n(b) the best interests of the person as a primary consideration.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) To avoid doubt, the express reference in paragraph (2)(d) to an\nancillary offence does not imply that references in\nparagraphs (2)(a), (b) or (c) to an offence do not include references\nto ancillary offences.\nEntering reasons in court records if court grants bail\n\n(3AAA) If the bail authority is a court and it grants bail, the court must:\n\n(a) state its reasons; and\n\n(b) cause those reasons to be entered in the court’s records.\nDetermining exceptional circumstances in relation to persons\nunder 18 years of age\n\n(3AA) In determining whether exceptional circumstances exist to justify\ngranting bail to a person who is under 18 years of age, without\nlimiting the matters the bail authority may have regard to, the bail\nauthority must have regard to:\n\n(a) the protection of the community as the paramount\nconsideration; and\n\n(b) the best interests of the person as a primary consideration.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15aa"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15aa-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15aa-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cf7855090da483e481f673347144783249e9fde13812f7541693a7685d58282b",
      "skos:note": "Court must state reasons for granting bail and cause them to be entered in court records.",
      "dc:description": "Reasons for granting bail"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15aa-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15AA(3) Bail not to be granted in certain cases",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 340,
      "values:originalText": "(3) To avoid doubt, the express reference in paragraph (2)(d) to an\nancillary offence does not imply that references in\nparagraphs (2)(a), (b) or (c) to an offence do not include references\nto ancillary offences.\nEntering reasons in court records if court grants bail\n\n(3AAA) If the bail authority is a court and it grants bail, the court must:\n\n(a) state its reasons; and\n\n(b) cause those reasons to be entered in the court’s records.\nDetermining exceptional circumstances in relation to persons\nunder 18 years of age\n\n(3AA) In determining whether exceptional circumstances exist to justify\ngranting bail to a person who is under 18 years of age, without\nlimiting the matters the bail authority may have regard to, the bail\nauthority must have regard to:\n\n(a) the protection of the community as the paramount\nconsideration; and\n\n(b) the best interests of the person as a primary consideration."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15aa-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
