    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ab-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15AB(4) Matters to be considered in certain bail applications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ab-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.346",
      "values:originalText": "(4) To avoid doubt, except as provided by subsections (1), (2) and\n(3A), this section does not affect:\n\n(a) any other matters that a bail authority must, must not or may\ntake into consideration in determining whether to grant bail\nor in determining conditions to which bail should be subject;\nor\n\n(b) the operation of a law of a State or a Territory.\nNote:\nSubsections (1) and (2) indirectly affect laws of the States and\nTerritories because they affect section 68 of the Judiciary Act 1903.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) To avoid doubt, except as provided by subsections (1), (2) and\n(3A), this section does not affect:\n\n(a) any other matters that a bail authority must, must not or may\ntake into consideration in determining whether to grant bail\nor in determining conditions to which bail should be subject;\nor\n\n(b) the operation of a law of a State or a Territory.\nNote:\nSubsections (1) and (2) indirectly affect laws of the States and\nTerritories because they affect section 68 of the Judiciary Act 1903.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ab"
      },
