        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a9b09758877963739b24fc292cbf98d8235861aaec082741971c49c753355669",
      "skos:note": "Matters to be considered in certain bail applications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ab-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15AB(4) Matters to be considered in certain bail applications",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 346,
      "values:originalText": "(4) To avoid doubt, except as provided by subsections (1), (2) and\n(3A), this section does not affect:\n\n(a) any other matters that a bail authority must, must not or may\ntake into consideration in determining whether to grant bail\nor in determining conditions to which bail should be subject;\nor\n\n(b) the operation of a law of a State or a Territory.\nNote:\nSubsections (1) and (2) indirectly affect laws of the States and\nTerritories because they affect section 68 of the Judiciary Act 1903."
    },
