      "values:originalText": "(1A) Where there is a law of a State or Territory with respect to the\nenforcement or recovery of fines ordered to be paid by offenders\n(including a law described in subsection (1AA)) that applies in\nrelation to fines ordered to be paid by offenders convicted by\ncourts of summary jurisdiction:\n\n(a) subsection (1) operates to require that law to apply and be\napplied to persons who are convicted summarily of federal\noffences by a federal court in the same manner as that law\nwould apply and be applied if the federal court were a court\nof summary jurisdiction; and\n\n(b) that subsection does not operate in relation to any law of that\nState or Territory that applies in relation to fines ordered to\nbe paid by offenders convicted by superior courts.",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) Where there is a law of a State or Territory with respect to the\nenforcement or recovery of fines ordered to be paid by offenders\n(including a law described in subsection (1AA)) that applies in\nrelation to fines ordered to be paid by offenders convicted by\ncourts of summary jurisdiction:\n\n(a) subsection (1) operates to require that law to apply and be\napplied to persons who are convicted summarily of federal\noffences by a federal court in the same manner as that law\nwould apply and be applied if the federal court were a court\nof summary jurisdiction; and\n\n(b) that subsection does not operate in relation to any law of that\nState or Territory that applies in relation to fines ordered to\nbe paid by offenders convicted by superior courts.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15a-ss-1a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15a-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15a-ss-1a-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15a-ss-1a-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15a-ss-1a-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "76e242091685bb602385088b6951a69969f9b084e7afaf18e9af0bc184c5ad16",
      "skos:note": "Law of a State or Territory applies to federal courts in relation to fines ordered to be paid by offenders convicted summarily."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15a-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15A(1A) Enforcement of fines etc.",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 348,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) Where there is a law of a State or Territory with respect to the\nenforcement or recovery of fines ordered to be paid by offenders\n(including a law described in subsection (1AA)) that applies in\nrelation to fines ordered to be paid by offenders convicted by\ncourts of summary jurisdiction:\n\n(a) subsection (1) operates to require that law to apply and be\napplied to persons who are convicted summarily of federal\noffences by a federal court in the same manner as that law\nwould apply and be applied if the federal court were a court\nof summary jurisdiction; and\n\n(b) that subsection does not operate in relation to any law of that\nState or Territory that applies in relation to fines ordered to\nbe paid by offenders convicted by superior courts."
    },
