    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15b-ss-1b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15B(1B) Time for commencement of prosecutions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15b-ss-1b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.351",
      "values:originalText": "(1B) A prosecution of an individual for an offence that is taken to have\nbeen committed because of section 11.2 or 11.2A of the Criminal\nCode, or against another law of the Commonwealth dealing with\naiding and abetting, in relation to an offence committed by a body\ncorporate may be commenced as follows:\n\n(a) if the maximum penalty which may be imposed for the\nprincipal offence in respect of a body corporate is, or\nincludes, a fine of more than 150 penalty units in the case of\na first conviction—at any time;\n\n(b) in any other case—at any time within one year after the\ncommission of the offence by the individual.",
      "skos:definition": "(1B) A prosecution of an individual for an offence that is taken to have\nbeen committed because of section 11.2 or 11.2A of the Criminal\nCode, or against another law of the Commonwealth dealing with\naiding and abetting, in relation to an offence committed by a body\ncorporate may be commenced as follows:\n\n(a) if the maximum penalty which may be imposed for the\nprincipal offence in respect of a body corporate is, or\nincludes, a fine of more than 150 penalty units in the case of\na first conviction—at any time;\n\n(b) in any other case—at any time within one year after the\ncommission of the offence by the individual.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15b-ss-1b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15b-ss-1b-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15b-ss-1b-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c30950083b1eca2d235c0d2bbea5d2d50bbe0b5df10d93a7dae6f93885596c1c",
      "skos:note": "Prosecution timing restrictions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15b-ss-1b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15B(1B) Time for commencement of prosecutions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 351,
      "values:originalText": "(1B) A prosecution of an individual for an offence that is taken to have\nbeen committed because of section 11.2 or 11.2A of the Criminal\nCode, or against another law of the Commonwealth dealing with\naiding and abetting, in relation to an offence committed by a body\ncorporate may be commenced as follows:\n\n(a) if the maximum penalty which may be imposed for the\nprincipal offence in respect of a body corporate is, or\nincludes, a fine of more than 150 penalty units in the case of\na first conviction—at any time;\n\n(b) in any other case—at any time within one year after the\ncommission of the offence by the individual."
    },
